  // ── The class reunion: name tags, old stories and the hard core (part243) ──
  //
  // Anekdote is not anedota. In Portuguese an anedota is a joke with a
  // punchline, and this pack means the story about the school trip — história.
  // That is a false friend that would have gone unnoticed, because the wrong
  // word is a real word and reads perfectly well.
  //
  // Die mit den Einsen becomes a dos vintes: Portugal marks out of twenty and
  // a vinte is the top of it, so the pupil German remembers by a grade is
  // remembered here by a different number that means the same thing.
