  "Was für eine Erleichterung.": "Que alívio.",

  // ── Cleaning: the mop, the limescale and the streaks on the glass (part251) ──
  //
  // Der Wischmopp is a esfregona, which is the object itself in Portugal and
  // not a description of it, and wischen is passar o pano, because Portuguese
  // names the cloth rather than the motion. Der Wasserkocher is o jarro
  // elétrico, the appliance as it is sold there.
  //
  // Sauber genug ist auch sauber only works if the second half sounds like a
  // verdict. Limpo que chegue também é limpo puts chegar where German put
  // genug, and the sentence ends the same way — with permission to stop.
  "staubwischen": "limpar o pó",
  "der Wischmopp": "a esfregona",
  "schrubben": "esfregar",
  "der Lappen": "o pano",
  "der Eimer": "o balde",
  "die Grundreinigung": "a limpeza a fundo",
  "der Kalk": "o calcário",
  "wischen": "passar o pano",
  "der Staubsauger": "o aspirador",
  "der Schwamm": "a esponja",
  "blitzblank": "a brilhar",
  "das Putzmittel": "o detergente",
  "der Staub": "o pó",
  "die Streifen": "as marcas",
  "Samstags wird bei uns geputzt.": "Cá em casa limpa-se ao sábado.",
  "Erst aufräumen, dann putzen — anders geht es nicht.": "Primeiro arrumar, depois limpar — de outra maneira não dá.",
  "Ich sauge, du wischst?": "Eu aspiro, tu passas o pano?",
