  // ── Parents' evening: tutoring, the oral mark and which school (part268) ──
  //
  // Nachhilfe is explicações, the word every Portuguese family uses, and the
  // person who gives them is o explicador. Förderunterricht is apoio ao
  // estudo, which is on the timetable of every Portuguese school, and the
  // Elternsprecher is o representante dos pais, the same unpaid job.
  //
  // The three school types keep their German names in the card that lists
  // them, because that card is about a German fork in the road that Portugal
  // does not have. The headwords say what each one is instead — o Gymnasium is
  // the liceu, the route to university, and that is the part a parent needs.
  "das Elterngespräch": "a reunião com o professor",
  "die Nachhilfe": "as explicações",
  "das Gymnasium": "o liceu",
  "die Realschule": "a via intermédia do secundário",
  "die Gesamtschule": "a escola secundária integrada",
  "der Elternsprecher": "o representante dos pais",
  "das Halbjahreszeugnis": "a avaliação do primeiro semestre",
  "nachsitzen": "ficar de castigo depois das aulas",
  "der Förderunterricht": "o apoio ao estudo",
  "überfordert": "perdido",
  "die Klassenkasse": "o fundo da turma",
  "mitarbeiten": "participar nas aulas",
