  // ── Children's illnesses: the fever, the rash and the paediatrician (part302) ──
  //
  // A Portuguese parent says borbulhas for a rash on a child, not erupção
  // cutânea, which belongs on a prescription. Das Bäuchlein is a barriguinha —
  // the same diminutive doing the same softening — and schlapp is mole.
  //
  // The U-Untersuchung keeps its name and gains a description, because it is a
  // numbered German appointment somebody has to book by name, and U7 means
  // nothing without it. Kita is a creche, which is the same institution with
  // the same opening hours and the same rule about fever.
  "die Windpocken": "a varicela",
  "der Kinderarzt": "o pediatra",
  "der Ausschlag": "as borbulhas",
  "ansteckend": "contagioso",
