  // ── Comfort calls, sleep and what you believe (part53) ──────────────────
  //
  // Schnarchen is ressonar, as everywhere else in this table, and ein
  // Nickerchen is uma sesta. Verschlafen has no verb of its own: não acordar a
  // horas is what somebody says on the phone at ten past nine.
  //
  // Toi, toi, toi exists because German will not say good luck out loud.
  // Portuguese has no such taboo, so the card is simply boa sorte — the
  // superstition is German and does not travel, but the wish does.
