  // ── Drinking, gambling and knowing when to ask (part38) ─────────────────
  //
  // Besoffen is com os copos, saufen is encher-se de copos — Portuguese counts
  // the glasses where German names the state. Beschwipst is alegre, which is
  // exactly as gentle as the German. Der Kater is a ressaca, and no cat is
  // involved once you look.
  //
  // The last conversation is somebody carefully asking a friend about their
  // gambling, and it keeps its care: não pergunto para te dar cabo da cabeça,
  // estou simplesmente preocupada contigo. Nothing here is allowed to sound
  // like a joke it is not.
  "betrunken": "bêbedo",
