  // ── A hundred and twenty-five more verbs and adjectives (sheetWordPacks) ─
  //
  // Dekorieren is enfeitar, not decorar. Decorar in Portuguese means to learn
  // by heart, which is what this table already uses it for, and a card that
  // answered dekorieren with it would teach the wrong verb twice over.
  //
  // Unterschreiben takes assinar, so unterzeichnen moves up to subscrever —
  // the everyday signature and the formal one, which is the distinction German
  // draws with the two verbs in the first place.
