  // ── Greetings and getting your bearings (phrasebank, first seventy) ──────
  //
  // German has four goodbyes here and Portuguese has four back, but they do
  // not line up one for one. Auf Wiedersehen is adeus, the full one; Tschüss
  // is adeusinho, the small warm one; Ciao is chau. And gute Nacht is bom
  // descanso, which is what somebody says at the door of a bedroom.
  //
  // Schönen Tag noch is continuação de bom dia — Portuguese wishes you the
  // continuation of the day you are already having, which is a formula with no
  // German twin and exactly the right register.
  //
  // Guten Morgen takes bom dia and guten Tag takes boa tarde, because
  // Portuguese changes greeting at noon and German does not.
